    <age name="ChisoPreniv">
        <set name="Journals">
            <element name="DniDictDE1">
                <translation language="English"><![CDATA[<cover src="DniDictDE1.hsm"><font size=12 style=b face=courier color=000000><margin right=56 left=56 top=40 bottom=40><PB><p align=center>

D'ni to English Dictionary: A-I<PB><PB>

<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>Abbreviations<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>

                   adj: adjective
                   adv: adverb
                   art: article
                   aux: auxiliary
                    cf: compare
                  conj: conjunction
                determ: determinative
                   fut: future
                     n: noun
                   num: number
                  perf: perfect
                  pers: person
                  plur: plural
                  pref: prefix
                  prep: preposition
                  pres: present
                  prog: progressive
                  pron: pronoun
               quantif: quantifier
                  sing: singular
                  suff: suffix
                     v: verb<PB><PB>

<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>A

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>advuh [åDvu] n., arch.

-ah [-a] suff., imperative.

ah [a] prep., marks an object directly affected by the action of the verb. Uses:
* in contrast with the recipient or goal marked by b';
* in contrast with the purpose marked by khe;
* when direct object is the subject of a subordinate clause.

ahbtsee [abxE] n., basalt.

ahbtseeets [abxEex] adj., basaltic.

ahchah [aca] n., sun(?), air(?), climate(?).

ahgo [ago] adj./adv., well.

-ahl [-al] suff., verb to adjective ("-ing", "-ed").

ahl [al] n., branch(?), leaf(?), blossom(?), flower(?).

-ahloth [-aloT] suff., verb to noun (one who endures an action or state).

-ahm [-am] suff., man(?), member(?). Telookahm "Surveyor".

-ahn [-an] suff., augmentative or intensive ending in certain nouns, verbs, and adjectives describing extensive, thorough, or deep states or processes.

ahn [an] n., body of water(?).

ahnee [anE] v., become, get.

ahneem [anEm] adj., fluid.

ahno [ano] n., water.

ahnoets [anoex] adj., watery, wet.

Ahnonay [anonA], lit. "Water Root".

ahnotahm [anotam] n., lava; magma-based.

ahreeuh [arEu] v., protect.

ahreeuhtahn [arEutan] n., protector.

ahreeuhtahv [arEutav] n., protection.

ahro [aro] adj., other, different.

ahrotahn [arotan] n., outsider, outworlder.

ahroy [arO] v., attend(?).

ahrtah [arta] v., allow(?), permit(?), let(?), do(?), cause(?).

ahtmay [atmA] v., stop(?), remove(?).

ahtsoo [axU] adj., ready.

ahve [ave] n., error.

ahyo [ayo] n., icon, symbol.

ahyoheek [ayohEK], D'ni game very similar to rock-paper-scissors.

Aitrus [Atrus], a D'ni name, actually spelled the same as Atrus.

al [ål] n., branch.

altee [åltE] n., branches.

altee rilerilonin [åltE rilerilonin] n., unexplored branches.

atinor [åtinor] n., beauty.

atinoret [åtinoret] adj., beautiful.

Atrus [Atrus], a D'ni name, actually spelled the same as Aitrus.

ayshoyk [ASOK] v., realize.

ayts'day [Ax'DA] n., retribution.

<PB><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>B

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>b [b-] prep., to.

bah [ba] n., beast.

bahkh [bak] adj., baked(?) (see chor bahkh).

bahn [ban] n., land(?) (see bahntahno).

bahntahno [bantano] n., island.

bahr [bar], craft(?), strength(?), energy(?).

bahrel [barel] v., make.

bahreltahn [bareltan] n., Maker, God.

bahreltahv [bareltav] n., (something) made.

bahro [baro] n., bahro; beast-people, enslaved ahrotahntee. Rarely spelled bah'ro.

bahronet [baronet] adj., phosphorescent.

bahrtah [barta] v., accomplish(?).

bahsh/bash [baS/båS] v., sense(?).

bahtsahnah [baxana] n., map.

bahtsen [baxen] v., map.

bahtsentahn [baxentan] n., cartographer.

bahvahnin [bavanin] adj., hidden.

bantee [båntE] n., series (seemingly always plural).

baykh [bAk] v., link, use a book to travel between Ages.

b'bree [b'brE] quantif., a little (lit. "to two").

be [be] prep., to.

beerah [bEra] v., keep, stay, remain.

beeree [bErE] v., maintain.

beereetahn [bErEtan] n., Maintainer.

bek [beK] n., game.

bekhe [beke] v., compel, force.

bel [bel] v., claim.

beletsahrah [belexara] n., plant similar to a lechuguilla agave.

bel'khah [bel'ka] adj., strange.

behn [ben] prep., for (exchange or duration).

bezol [bezol] v., trap.

bezol pumi [bezol pumE?] n., a carnivorous plant clinging on trees, native to Negilahn. Its preys are the pumi.

b'fahsee [b'fasE] quantif., as much as possible (lit. "to twenty-five").

bigto [bigto] n., blessing.

bintah [binta] n., law, ordinance.

birahno [birano] n., sea. Birahnokh Rintotee "Sea of Dreams".

bishtah [biSta] n., tunnel.

biv [biv] determ., all, every.

bivdil [bivDil] pron., everything.

bivrov [bivrov] pron., everyone.

-blo [-blo] num., 25^5 (=9,765,625), combining form.

blo [blo] prep., about.

bo- [bo-] pref., simple fut. tense ("will write").

bodo- [boDo-] pref., fut. prog. tense ("will be writing").

bodol- [boDol-] pref., fut. perf. prog. tense ("will have been writing").

boko- [boKo-] pref., fut. perf. tense ("will have written") (see bol-). Perhaps intentional rather than predictive of a future state.

bol [bol] n., brother.

bol- [bol-] pref., fut. perf. tense ("will have written").

bonoo [bonU] n., acid.

bonooets [bonUex] adj., acidic.

boogin [bUgin] n., creature.

bor [bor] n., page, specifically of the special paper used in Linking Books.

borin [borin] adj., tired.

bortah [borta] n., purpose(?).

bre- [bre-] prep., to the (b' + re-).

bree [brE] num., 2, two.

bren [bren] n., millennium.

b'rigahsen [b'rigasen] quantif., highly (lit. "to twenty-three").

b'rish [b'riS] quantif., so, very (lit. "to twenty").

broon [brUn] n., tube.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>C

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>cannen [Kånen?] n., a device for playing recorded music.

chahg [cag] v., add.

chahn [can] v., can, be able to, may.

chay [cA] n., fault (geological).

cheecho [cEco] n., temperate grassland biome.

cheereetahn [cErEtan] n., animal native to Sameehn, undomesticated.

cheereelay [cErElA] n., animal native to Sameehn, domesticated.

cheto [ceto] n., disposition.

chev [cev] n./v., thank.

chevet [cevet] adj., thankful.

chevtahvtee [cevtavtE] n., thanks.

chil [cil] adj., main.

chilesh [cileS] adv., mainly.

chir [cir] n., organism.

chiso [ciso] v., archive.

Chiso Preniv [ciso preniv], lit. "Another Archive".

chisotahn [cisotan] n., archivist.

choohah [cUha] v., catch.

choor [cUr] v., learn.

chor bahkh [cor bak] n., baked roll, a type of D'ni food.

choylahnay [cOlanA] v., complete.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>D

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>d'/de- [D'/De-] adv., again, re-.

dahbah [Daba] v., tell.

dahbahn [Daban] n., cannister(?), alembic(?); a device used by Gehn to lit up his pipe.

dahg [Dag] v., strike.

dahgo [Dago] n., hammer.

dah'ko, dahko [DaKo] n., marble.

dahsh [DaS] n., dome towers in Riven.

dahtahm [Datam] n., firemarble.

Dahtahmnay [DatamnA], lit. "Firemarble Root" (dah'ko + tahm + nay).

Dakotah, misspelling of Tokotah.

dayjee [DAjE] n., path.

dayjee fahlah'ahl [DAjE fala'al] n., labyrinth (unicursal); lit. "folded path".

de- [De-] adv., again, re-.

delahn [Delan] n., sky.

delin [Delin] adj./n., misty; mist.

Demath [DimaT] n., a D'ni name.

dereno [Dereno] n., ice, tundra.

deretheni [DereTenE] n., a jet black, light weight, artificial stone.

deseekay [DesEKA] n., puzzle, enigma.

devokan [DevoKån] n., hope.

dhaynoy [dAnO] n., setback.

dhelim [delim] n., right, legal claim.

dho [do] adv., how.

dhozonesh [dozoneS] adv., however(?).

dil [Dil] n., thing.

direbo [Direbo] n., wheel.

D'ni [D'nE], lit. "New Start".

do- [Do-] pref., pres. prog. tense
(_ing; am/is/are _ing).

dol- [Dol-] pref., pres. perf. prog. tense
(have been _/has been _).

don [Don] adv., like, as if it were.

doo [DU] n., food.

doo'shol [DU'Sol] n., cater.

doo'sholtahn [DU'Soltan] n., caterer.

doren [Doren] n., dug out structure(?).

dormahdh [Dormad] v., defeat.

dovah [Dova] n., world.

doyhah [DOha] n., machine.

drahtol [Dratol] n., guest.

duh [Du] n., food.

<PB><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>E

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>eder [eDer] n./v., sleep, rest. In Age names, identifies Garden Ages.

eder tomahn [eDer toman] n., way station, rest house.

een [En] pron./det., any.

eer [Er] n., bandage (strip of cloth to cover a wound).

eest [Est] pron., them; 3rd pers. plur. object pronoun.

-eet [-Et] suff., 3rd pers. plur. actor ("they").

el [el] adj., high (see Relto).

elahth [elaT] n., highest one(?), proud one(?), elite(?).

eleeahn [elEan] n., upper class(?).

eleeahnith [elEaniT] n., upper class member(?), refugee(?), exile(?).

elemahr [elemar] n., spore.

elioykh [eliOk] n., gust.

elioykhets [eliOkex] adj., gusty.

elon [elon] v., raise(?), uplift(?), elevate(?).

elonet [elonet] adj., uplifting(?), elevated(?).

-em [-em] suff., 2nd pers. sing. actor ("you").

emee [emE] v., win.

-en [-en] suff., 3rd pers. sing. actor ("he", "she", "it").

enday [enDA] v., build.

endaytahn [enDAtan] n., builder.

entahn(?) [entan] n., honesty(?), worth(?).
This word is only known through an unclear audio recording, the spelling is uncertain.

enyahlo [enyalo] adj., sick.

enyahloth [enyaloT] n., sickly one.

er' [er'], a common prefix for Ages used by the Guild of Caterers for harvesting food (e.g. Er'cana, Er'duna, Er'jera).

erem [erem] n., skill.

erth [erT] art., a, an.

-esh [-eS] suff., adjective to adverb ("-ly").

-et [-et] suff., 1st pers. plur. actor ("we").

-et [-et] suff., noun to adjective ("-ful") (cf. -ets, -t).

etahf [etaf] n., seed.

-eth [-eT] suff., adjective to noun ("-ty", "_ one") (cf. -th).

-ets [-ex] suff., noun to adjective ("-y", "-th") (cf. -et, -t).


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>F

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>f' [f'] prep., on (cf. fe-, fre-).

fah [fa] num., 1, one; single.

fahdho [fado] n., experience.

fahets [faex] adj., first.

fahlah [fala] v., fold.

fahm [fam] adj./adv., far.

fahmon [famon] v., push back, oppose.

fahsee [fasE] num., 25, twenty-five.

fahsh [faS] adj., near.

fe- [fe-] prep., on, upon.

fel [fel] n., paddle, oar.

fel [fel] v., row.

feltahn [feltan] n., rower, one who rows a boat.

fenah [fena] n., story.

fenges [fenges] v., act, playing a role.

fengestahn [fengestan] n., actor, a person who plays a role.

fengestoy [fengestO] n., acting, the art of playing a role.

fentahsentah [fentasenta] n., historian.

ferem [ferem] adj., dry.

feshkin [feSKin] v., guide.

feshkintahn [feSKintan] n., one who guides.

filahdh [filad] n., top.

fitay [fitA] v., look.

flin [flin] n., order, condition.

foles [foles] v., wait.

fooruh [fUru] adj., sufficient.

foosah [fUsa] v., call.

foosahtahv [fUsatav] n., name.

fre [fre] prep., at the, on the.

fuhsh [fuS], switch(?); choice(?); crystal(?).




<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>G

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>g'/gah [g'/ga] conj., and (cf. gre-).

gahlon [galon] n., ground.

gahlpo [galpo] n., cave.

gahn [gan] n., empire.

gahrahno [garano] n., ocean.

Gahreesen [garEsen], lit. "Mighty Protective Structure" (gahro-ahreeuh-senaren).

gahrkahl [garKal] n., storm.

gahrkahlets [garKalex] adj., stormy.

gahro [garo] adj., great, in might or importance.

gahrohevtee [garohevtE] n., Great Words, a special set of words for writing Ages.

gahrosh [garoS] adv., mightily, greatly.

gahroth [garoT] n., greatness, great one.

gahrtahvo [gartavo] n., equal to ~6 hr 3 min. Divided into 25 tahvotee.

Gahrternay [garternA], lit. "Root of the Great Tree".

gahth [gaT] adv., still, yet.

gahtsai [gaxA?] n., tiger-bat, an animal native to Negilahn. The tarpin shal lifecycle is connected to the gahtsai.

gatah [gåta] adj., due.

ge'dahn [ge'Dan] n., wisdom.

gedee [geDE] n., surprise(?), setback(?).

gel [gel] v., write (ordinary) (cf. rilgelin "unwritten").

geltahn [geltan] n., writer (cf. seltahn "Writer").

geltahv [geltav] n., written work, prophetic book or writings.

Geltovokum [geltovoKum] n., the Temple to Yahvo.

gemedet [gemeDet] n., six-in-a-line, a D'ni game played on a 3D grid.

Gehn [gen] n., a D'ni name.

gerah [gera] n., sun.

gerahn(o) [gerano] n., foundation(?), strength(?), nourishment(?).

gestoy [gestO] n., the Art.

Ghen, misspelling of Gehn.

gid [giD] v., excavate.

gidtahv [giDtav] n., excavation.

gilo [gilo] n., plant.

gimit [gimit] adj., immediate.

gipeli [gipelE?] n., jelly-fly, a small, colorful animal native to Negilahn.

girah [gira] n., steam(?).

gitsah [gixa] adj., safe.

gitsahth [gixaT] n., safety.

glahs [glas] v., drink.

glo [glo] v., begin.

go [go] n., soup.

gol [gol] n., arm (body part).

golah [gola] n., justice(?).

golahntahn [golantan] n., judge. Regolahntahnteeokh Yahvo, the Judges of Yahvo.

gonahth [gonaT] n., poor one(?), servant(?), slave(?).

gopah [gopa] conj., because.

gor [gor] n., time.

gorahn [goran] n., unit of time equal to ~35 sec. Divided into 25 prorahntee.

gorahyan [gorayån] n., clock.

gormet [gormet] adv., now (lit. "this time").

gormot [gormot] adv., then (lit. "that time").

gorven [gorven] adv., soon.

goyray [gOrA] adv., straight.

grahner [graner] n., path.

g're-/gre- [g're-/gre-] conj., and the (cf. gah "and").

guhlem [gulem] n., strait.

Guhlem Shahveroo n., Dire Strait.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>H

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>hahpo [hapo] v., combine, mix.

hahr [har] n., equal to one mean solar year. Divided into 10 vaileetee.

hahrtah [harta] n., cycle.

hahrtah choylahnaytahv [harta cOlanAtav] n., anniversary (lit. "complete cycle").

hahrten [harten] v., circle.

hahzah [haza] adj., white.

hayvuh [hAvu] n., savanna, tropical grassland.

hee- [hE-] num., 15, fifteen, combining form.

heebor [hEbor] num., 15, fifteen.

heegahbree [hEgabrE] num., 17, seventeen.

heegahfah [hEgafa] num., 16, sixteen.

heegahsen [hEgasen] num., 18, eighteen.

heegahtor [hEgator] num., 19, nineteen.

heek [hEK] n., cane; Gehn's rifle.

her [her] n., number.

hern [hern] n., room.

hev [hev] n., word.

hevkor [hevKor] n., lexicon, dictionary (lit. "word-book").

hevo [hevo] n., swarm.

hoor [hUr] v., find.

hoosahtay [hUsatA] adj., difficult(?), satisfied(?), successful(?).

hootsay [hUxA] adj., holy.

hootsayth [hUxAT] n., holiness.

hoshah [hoSa] n., cowardice.

h'rot [h'rot] n., tower.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>I

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>idhsay [idsA] n., line.

iglahrno [iglarno] adj., temporary.

-ij [-ij] suff., passive voice.

ikhah [ika] n., meat.

ikhah naijuhets [ika nIjuex] n., smoked meat.

ilaïs [ilåis] v., power, charge.

-in [-in] suff., passive participle ("-en", "-ed", "-t").

inaltahv [inåltav] n., opportunity(?), privilege(?).

inay [inA], more than.

irah [ira] n., darling, honey; endearment used with spouse or close friend.

irvan [irvån] n., mineral.

istah [ista] prep., through.

isyeer [isyEr] v., revere.]]></translation>
