<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>J

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>jahgah [jaga] v., warrant(?), provide(?).

Jahkooth [jåKUT] n., the D'ni Devil.

jahlahk [jalaK] n., pillar, column.

jayl [jAl] adj., equal.

Jenahkai [jenaKI] n., neighborhood in D'ni.

jeroo [jerU] adj., possible.

jerooth [jerUT] n., possibility.

jikhah [jika] v., remain.

jimah [jima] n., prophecy.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>K

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>Kadish [KADiS] n., a D'ni name.

kahg [Kag] adj., original.

kahgesh [KageS] adv., originally.

kahlo [Kalo] n., wind, breeze.

kahnrad [KanråD] v., think.

kahntin [Kantin] v., oppress.

kahntinahloth [KantinaloT] n., oppressed one.

kahntintahn [Kantintan] n., oppressor.

kahzee [KazE] v., detour.

kailo [KIlo] v., bring.

kaligo [Kåligo] n., council.

kam [Kåm] pron., what.

kamdol [KåmDol] adv., why.

kamfah [Kåmfa] pron., which (lit. "what one").

kamrov [Kåmrov] pron., who, whom (lit. "what person").

kamto [Kåmto] adv./conj., where (lit. "what place").

kanen [Kånen] n., cannen, a device for playing recorded music.

kat [Kåt] adv., only, just.

Kadish [KADiS], a D'ni name.

keebah [KEba] v., obey.

keelah [KEla] v., spend(?), pass(?), endure(?).

keelen [KElen] n., step.

keemo [KEmo] n., a kind of fish native to Eder Kemo.

kelahnee [KelanE] n., antelope.

ken [Ken] v., be.

kerah [Kera] adj., brave.

kerahth [KeraT] n., brave one.

keshtahv [KeStav] n., caution, warning.

keso [Keso] v., change.

kesotahn [Kesotan] n., changer.

kesotahv [Kesotav] n., change.

kevo [Kevo] adj., another, in addition to.

kevoth [KevoT] n., another, one who is another.

kh' [k'] prep., for (cf. khe-).

khah [ka] adj., few.

khahg [kag] v., choose.

khahntor/khantor [kantor/kåntor] v., reflect(?), contemplate(?), concentrate(?).

khahpo [kapo] adv., perhaps.

khe- [ke-] prep., for (cf. kh').

khlay/klay [klA/KlA] n., example.

khoy [kO] conj., if.

khoyoo [koyU] v., invoke.

khoytahg/khoytag [kOtag/kOtåg] n., result(?), lesson(?), topic(?).

khre- [kre-] prep., for the (cf. khe-).

kino [Kino] v., fail.

kiri [Kiri?] n., krill fly or krill stag, an animal native to Negilahn. Urwins filter them from the air with their beaks.

kirin [Kirin] n., desert sand.

k'lahd [K'laD] n., sword.

klay [KlA] n., example.

ko- [Ko-] pref., simple past tense (did/-ed).

kobol- [Kobol-] pref., fut. past tense (would have).

kodo- [KoDo-] pref., past prog. (or passive) tense (was/were).

kodol- [KoDol-] pref., past perf. prog. tense (had been).

kol- [Kol-] pref., past perf. tense (had).

kooahn [KUan] n., stream.

koozah [KUza] v., surrender.

kor [Kor] n., book.

korbah [Korba] n., book-making.

korchis [Korcis] n., notebook.

korfah [Korfa] n., first book.

Korfah V'jah [Korfa v'ja] n., First Book Celebration.

korfeshkin [KorfeSKin] n., guidebook.

kormahn [Korman] n., descriptive book.

kor'neeah [Kor'nEa] n., blank book.

korvahkh [Korvak] n., linking book.

kosuh [Kosu] adj., many.

kotah [Kota] n./adj., locked door or having locked door(s).

kotsah [Koxa] n., gate.

kro [Kro] v., move.

kroges [Kroges] v., dance.

krogestahn [Krogestan] n., dancer.

krogestoy [KrogestO] n., dance, the art of dancing.

k'tesh [K'teS] v., entertain.

k'tsee [K'xE] adj., happy.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>L

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>l' [l'] pref., present perf. tense (has/have) before a vowel (see le-).

lahn [lan] adj., only.

-lahn [-lan] num., 25^3 (15,625), combining form.

lahsah [lasa] v., seal, close.

lahth [laT] n., highest ones(?), proud ones(?), elite(?) (see elahth).

laki [laKE] n., large aquatic animal native to Laki'ahn. They bear red gemstones in their bodies, which the Kresh harvested by fighting them in an arena before an audience of D'ni.

lan [lån] v., wear(?), gain(?).

laysoo [lAsU] v., carry.

laysootahn [lAsUtan] n., carrier, courier.

le- [le-] pref., present perf. tense (has/have). Loses the 'e' before a vowel (see l').

lee- [lE-] n., combining form of vailee in D'ni month names.

leeahm [lEam] n., question.

leekrotahn [lEKrotan] n., ferry boat.

leeshah [lESa], much(?), majority(?), most(?).

leeshahn [lESan] n., whole.

lelahm [lelåm] n., a plant "expanding in size but lessening in thickness" while it grows (Words).

lem [lem] n., ink used in Books (cf. tem "ordinary ink").

-len [-len] num., 25^3 (15,625), combining form, alternate (cf. -lahn).

lenah [lena] n., journey.

lenitah [lenita] n., idiot.

lensho [lenSo] v., tour.

lenshokintahn [lenSoKintan] n., tour guide.

lenshotahn [lenSotan] n., tourist.

lerilon [lerilon] v., explore.

lesah [lesa] adj., sealed.

lesh [leS] n., rule, fact.

lis [lis] v., arrive, get.

l'izchah [l'izca] v., cry.

lon [lon] v., discover.

lonep [lonep] n., discovery(?).

look [lUK] n., survey.

loopah [lUpa] n., risk(?), trip(?).

lorahg/lorag [lorag/loråg] n., grace(?), joy(?).

loymaht [lOmat] conj., though.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>M

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>mahdho/madho [mado/mådo] v., succeed(?), join(?), participate(?).

mahgen/magen [magen/mågen] n., powers(?), wonders(?).

mahlah [mala] v., come.

mahn [man] n., existence (cf. kormahn "descriptive book").

mahnshoo [manSU] v., die.

mahnshootahv [manSUtav] n., death.

mahnshootahvting [manSUtavting] n., death, mortality.

mahnshooth [manSUT] n., Death Bringer.

mahrah [mara] n. music(?), concert(?) (cf. tomahrah "concert hall").

mahrahnah [marana] n., concert.

mahrent [marent] v., follow.

mahrg [marg] n., layer.

mahrn [marn] v., create.

mahrntahn [marntan] n., creator.

mahrntahv [marntav] n., creation.

mahryayshah [maryASa] n., fan(?), devotee(?) (cf. yayshah "joy").

mahtahn [matan] v., leave(?), put aside(?), dismiss(?).

maiood [mIUD] n., means(?), tool(?), ability(?).

mairuh [mIru] v., own.

malo [målo] v., forget.

maral-obe [maral-obe] n., a woodwind musical instrument.

me [me] prep., from, of, made from.

mees [mEs] v., speak.

meestahn [mEstan] n., speaker.

meestahnyah [mEstanya] n., prophet.

meestahv [mEstav] n., speech.

meet [mEt] adv., there.

mefel [mefel] n., night.

megormot [megormot] adv., since (lit. from that time).

megoyray [megOrA] adv., straight out.

-mel [-mel] num., 25^4 (390,625), combining form.

melin [melin] adj., outer.

meoor [meUr] n., pleasure, (idiom) you're welcome.

mepord [meporD] n., prince(?).

mer [mer] v., watch (cf. todelmer "planetarium").

merk [merK] n., poisoned water.

merkchir [merKcir] n., disinfectant.

mes [mes] v., require.

met [met] pron., this, these; determ. this.

metee [metE] determ., these.

milesh [mileS] v., hug, embrace.

mileshtahv [mileStav] n., hug, embrace.

min [min] n., woman.

minkata [minKata] adj./n., heavily scarred.

miro [miro] adj., toxic.

misho [miSo] n., universe.

mishtah [miSta] v., construct.

mishtahtahv [miStatav] n., construction.

m'lah [m'la] n., lizard.

mo [mo] conj., that(?), the fact that(?).

mooden [mUDen] n., fortune.

mooshee [mUSE] n., communication(?), enthusiasm(?), terrain(?).

mor [mor] n., mother.

mor'okh'mor [mor'ok'mor] n., grandmother(?).

morokhpor [morokpor] n., paternal grandmother(?).

morpah [morpa] n., queen (cf. porpah "king").

mot [mot] pron., which, that; determ. that.

motee [motE] determ., those.

m're-/mre- [m're-/mre-] prep., from the, of the.

muhkhon [mukon] adj., complex, complicated.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>N

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>n' [n'] prep., around.

na'grenis [nå'grenis] adj., brittle.

nahdahn [naDan] n., mushroom.

nahdahnets [naDanex] adj., mushroomy (cf. Teledahn).

nahgah [naga] v., reward.

nahn [nan] v., act, perform an action.

nahntahv [nantav] n., action.

nahr [nar] adj., significant.

nahrah [nara] n., nara, the hardest of substances manufactured by the D'ni.

nahsh [naS] n., part(?).

nahvah [nava] n., master.

naijuh [nIju] n., smoke.

naijuhets [nIjuex] adj., smoked (cf. ikhah naijuhets "smoked meat").

nay [nA] n., root.

nay- [nA-] num., 10, ten, combining form.

naygahbree [nAgabrE] num., 12, twelve.

naygahfah [nAgafa] num., 11, eleven.

naygahsen [nAgasen] num., 13, thirteen.

naygahtor [nAgator] num., 14, fourteen.

nayvoo [nAvU] num., 10, ten.

ne [ne] prep., around.

nee [nE] adj., new, fresh, clean.

neeah [nEa] adj., new, blank.

neeg [nEg] adj., mere.

neegesh [nEgeS] adv., merely.

neemah [nEma] v., annoy, pester.

neetsahvay [nExavA] v., suffer.

negilahn [negilan] n., jungle, rainforest.

nekis [neKis] v., bend, twist, distort.

nekisahl [neKisal] adj., bent, twisted, distorted.

nekisahloth [neKisaloT] n., bent, twisted, distorted one.

nem [nem] v., form (make or create).

nerim [nerim] n., colorpillar, a caterpillar-like animal native to Negilahn. They are eaten by reepah.

neseet [nesEt] adv., almost(?).

netso [nexo] v., produce, make.

neze [neze] v., read.

nezetahn [nezetan] n., reader.

nogin [nogin] v., scatter(?), separate(?), ignore(?).

noref [noref] adj., final.

nuhdah [nuDa] v., hinder(?), obstruct(?).

nuhdahtahv [nuDatav] n., hindrance(?), obstruction(?), disaster(?).

nuhree [nurE] n., nure, the primary D'ni monetary unit (cf. pradnuhreetee).


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>O

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>oenahzo [oenazo] v., hope, wish.

ogel [ogel] v., age, get old(?).

oglahn [oglan] adj., ancient.

-okh [-ok] prep., of, belonging to. Used as a separate word when the thing possessed is a phrase.

oko [oKo] adj., black.

-om [-om] suff., 2nd sing. possessor ("your").

-omee [-omE] suff., 2nd plur. possessor ("your").

omsheeno [omSEno] n., rails, track.

-on [-on] suff., 3rd sing. possessor
("his", "her", "its").

oner [oner] adj., just, fair.

oochah [Uca] n., worm.

oochah pahrah [Uca para] n., a young tarpin shal.

oolbah [Ulba] n., office.

oolin [Ulin] v., control(?), govern(?), master(?).

oolintahv [Ulintav] n., control(?), mastery(?).

ooloy [UlO] adj., tall.

oonahn [Unan] adj., hostile.

oonray [UnrA] n., lord.

ooshah [USa] n., formula.

-os [-os] suff., 3rd plur. possessor ("their").

oshahn [oSan] v., lose.

oshahnin [oSanin] adj., lost.

-ot [-ot] suff., 1st plur. possessor ("our").

-oy [-O] suff., 1st sing. possessor ("my").

oyn [On] prep., myself(?), for my sake(?), moreover(?).

oytahg [Otag] v., teach.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>P

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>p' [p'] prep., above.

pahboy [pabO] v., bless.

pahl [pal] adv., ever.

pahm [pam] conj., or.

pahn [pan] v., trust.

pahrah [para] adj., great,  in size or strength.

pahrahno [parano] n., sea(?) (lit. "large water").

pahrahth [paraT] n., greatness, largeness.

pahrkh [park] v., pray(?).

pahrtahvo [partavo], equal to ~1 hour 13 mins. Also known as "bell".

pahts [pax] n., city.

palmen [pålmen] n., magnet.

palmenets [pålmenex] adj., magnetic.

panuhdoy [pånuDO] n., an animal native to Negilahn, almost twice the height of an urwin. Also known as "big leg".

paychahvo [pAcavo] n., danger.

payiferen [pAiferen] n., desert (cf. paychahvo "danger", ferem "dry").

paypeel [pApEl] v., be upset(?), be distracted(?), anticipate(?).

pazgo [påzgo] v., [fund (by a grant)].

pe [pe] prep., above.

pekay [peKA] adj., insidious.

-per [-per] suff., "-ple", "-fold" (cf. senper "triple").

perah [pera] n., cacophony.

peray [perA] adj., silly.

pilel [pilel] v., receive.

pirelin [pirelin] n., village.

pirin [pirin] n., color.

pisho [piSo] v., belong.

po [po] n., mouth(?).

poahnt [poant] n., saliva.

po'aht [po'at] n., mouthful(?).

pod [poD] determ., each.

poget [poget] v., rule, reign.

poog [pUg] v., prove(?).

por [por] n., father.

porpah [porpa] n., king.

poy [pO] n., bulb.

prachiz [praciz/pråciz] v., amaze(?), astound(?).

prad [pråD] n., rock.

pradets [pråDex] adj., rocky.

pradges [pråDges] v., sculpt.

pradgestahn [pråDgestan] n., sculptor.

pradgestoy [pråDgestO] n., sculpture.

pradnuhreetee [pråDnurEtE] n., money stone, "in essence like a modern smart card" (cf. nuhree).

pradteegahl [pråDtEgal] adj., rock-working.

preniv [preniv] adv., once again.

prin [prin] adj., small.

prorahn [proran] n., unit of time equal to ~1.5 seconds.

pumi [pumE?] n., a monkey-like animal native to Negilahn, usually jumping from tree to tree. Also known as "two tails monkey".]]></translation>
            </element>
            <element name="DniDictDE3">
                <translation language="English"><![CDATA[<cover src="DniDictDE3.hsm"><font size=12 style=b face=courier color=000000><margin right=56 left=56 top=40 bottom=40><PB><p align=center>

D'ni to English Dictionary: R-Z<PB><PB>

<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>Abbreviations<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>

                   adj: adjective
                   adv: adverb
                   art: article
                   aux: auxiliary
                    cf: compare
                  conj: conjunction
                determ: determinative
                   fut: future
                     n: noun
                   num: number
                  perf: perfect
                  pers: person
                  plur: plural
                  pref: prefix
                  prep: preposition
                  pres: present
                  prog: progressive
                  pron: pronoun
               quantif: quantifier
                  sing: singular
                  suff: suffix
                     v: verb<PB><PB>

<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>R

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>r' [r'] art., the.

-rah [-ra] num., 25^2 (625), combining form.

rahm [ram] adj., good.

rahn [ran] v., [vary].

rahnahl [ranal] adj., various.

rahshah [raSa] adj., [dark].

rahshahth [raSaT] n., dark, darkness.

rahsoo [rasU] adj., vanquished.

rahwah [rawa] adj., meaningful, rich :)

raiway [rIwA] n., procedure.

Rakeri [raKerE], a D'ni name.

ran [rån] v., measure.

re- [re-] art., the/that.

Rebek [rebeK], lit. "The Game".

re'dahntee [re'DantE] n., long tweezers.

reekoo [rEKU] n., a small animal native to Ader Jamat.

reepah [rEpa] n., a timid, gorilla-like animal native to Negilahn, with a tail resembling a scorpion's. They eat nerim, gipeli and other plants and animals.

rees [rEs] v., eat.

reeslo [rEslo] v., dissolve.

reetahn [rEtan] n., survivor(?).

reethai [rETI] prep., during(?).

rek/rahk [reK/raK] n., class(?).

Relto [relto], lit. "the High Place" (re-el-to).

Relyimah [relyima] n./adj., Unseen, Terahnee slaves (cf. rilyimah).

rem [rem] v., flow.

remah [rema] n., north.

remesfet [remesfet] adj., diligent.

remesfeteth [remesfeteT] n., diligence.

rev [rev] n., right (direction).

ri- [ri-] num., 20, twenty, combining form.

rifeen [rifEn] v., torment.

rifoon [rifUn] v., remember.

rigahbree [rigabrE] num., 22, twenty-two.

rigahfah [rigafa] num., 21, twenty-one.

rigahsen [rigasen] num., 23, twenty-three.

rigahtor [rigator] num., 24, twenty-four.

rigilahs [rigilas] n., taiga, boreal forest.

ril [ril] determ., no, not.

rilahsah [rilasa] v., unseal.

rildil [rilDil] pron., nothing.

rilerilonin [rilerilonin] adj., unexplored (cf. lon "discover"). Altee Rilerilonin "Unexplored Branches".

rilgelin [rilgelin] adj., unwritten (cf. gel).

rilnahr [rilnar] adj., insignificant.

rilrov [rilrov] pron., nobody.

riltahgahmin [riltagamin] adj., unknown.

rilte [rilte] prep., without.

rilyimah [rilyima] adj., unseen (cf. Relyimah).

rinal [rinål] v., honor, venerate.

rinaltahv [rinåltav] n., [honor, veneration].

rinto [rinto] n., dream. Birahnokh Rintotee "Sea of Dreams".

rish [riS] num., 20, twenty.

riway [rIwA] n., procedure.

ro [ro] n. (Terahnee), people group, household, or family (e.g. Hadre Ro'Jethhe).

robot [robot] adj., actual.

rochay [rocA] v., reach.

Ronay [ronA], lit. "People of the Root".

roo [rU] conj., that.

rooay [rUA] n., route.

rooayk [rUAK] v., destroy.

rooayktahv [rUAKtav] n., destruction.

roob [rUb] conj., but.

roodsh [rUDS] adj., red.

roomay [rUmA] v., ignore(?), circumvent(?), alter(?).

roon [rUn] num., 0, zero.

roshee [roSE] n., crater.

rotee [rotE] n., peoples(?).

rov [rov] n., person.

rovhoo [rovhU] n., holy person, saint (cf. hootsay "holy").


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>S

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>saheth [saeT] n., sleep.

say [sA] n./v., design.

sayrah [sAra] n., west.

se [se] prep., at.

-see [-sE] num., 25, combining form.

seen [sEn] v., get, acquire.

sek/sekh [seK/sek] v., have, own.

sel [sel] v., Write (Ages).

seltahn [seltan] n., Writer, one who writes Ages.

sen [sen] num., 3, three.

senahren [senaren] n., building, structure.

senper [senper] adj., triple, threefold.

seraht [serat] v., light up, brighten.

seren [seren] n., light.

Serenol [serenol] n., Age where tuliema grow, written by Atrus.

set [set] pron., us.

sev [sev] n., Age.

-sh [-S] suff., adjective to adverb ("-ly").

shahfee [SafE] n., span, equal to 15.8 ft or 4.82 m. Twice the length of a pendulum with a period of 5 prorahntee is 5 spans.

shahl [Sal?] drop(?), extended below(?). Tarpin shal, an animal native to Negilahn, preying by dropping down from high branches on unsuspecting victims.

shahmlis [Samlis] adj., perfect.

shahn [San] v., connect, piece together (as in a puzzle).

shahveroo [SaverU] adj., dire. Guhlem Shahveroo "Dire Strait".

sheegah [SEga] n., way(?), path(?), passage(?).

sheemah [SEma] adj., okay, alright.

sheetem [SEtem] n., message.

sheetemsootahn [SEtemsUtan] n., messenger.

sheeyah [SEya] n., angel.

Shegahdah [SegaDa] n., neighborhood in D'ni.

shelah [Sela] v., (tran)scribe(?).

shelahtahn [Selatan] n., scribe.

shem [Sem] pron., you.

shento [Sento] v., take.

sheten [Seten] v., cherish.

shin [Sin] adj., able.

sho [So] n., dirt, soil.

shokhoo [SokU] v., instruct.

shokrotahn [SoKrotan] n., bulldozer (lit. "dirt-mover").

shol [Sol] v., prepare.

sholen [Solen] adj., drawn.

shooth [SUT] n., death.

shorah [Sora] n./interj., peace; hello, farewell.

shoraht [Sorat] adj., peaceful.
Hahr rahm gah shoraht "happy new year" (lit. "good and peaceful year").

shuhfay [SufA] v., finish.

shuhteejoo [SutEjU] n., rocksalt.

sifay [sifA] adj., wired.

sofeguh [sofegu] v., fear.

sol [sol] n., sister.

somah [soma] n., seal, signet.

soygi [sOgi] adj., stable.

soygish [sOgiS], mispelling of soygith.

soygith [sOgiT] n., stability.

stofah [stofa], of one.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>T

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>-t [-t] suff., noun to adjective ("-ful") (cf. -et, -ets).

t' [t'] prep., in, by, with (cf. te, terth-, tre-).

tah [ta] pron., it.

tahg [tag] v., give.

tahgahm [tagam] v., know.

tahgayr [tagAr] v., learn.

tahgil [tagil] v., understand.

Tahgirah [tagira] n., a prison Age (possibly tahg + girah).

tahleeo [talEo] n., surface.

tahm [tam] n., fire.

-tahn [-tan] suff., verb to noun ("-er", "-or", "-tor").

tahroo [tarU] v., die (by accident or murder).

tarpin shal [tarpin Sal?] n., drop claw, an animal native to Negilahn, preying by dropping down from high branches on unsuspecting victims. Oocha para is a young tarpin shal. The tarpin shal life cycle is connected to the gahtsai.

tahs [tas] v., muse, think, ponder, meditate.

-tahv [-tav] suff., verb to noun ("-ion", "-tion").

tahvo [tavo] n., unit of time equal to ~14.5 min. Divided into 25 gorahntee.

Takotah, misspelling of Tokotah.

tanuh [tånu] v., be blind(?), be injured(?).

tanuhth [tånuT] n., blindness(?), injury(?).

tay [tA] n., aim(?), goal(?) (cf. taykheboorkh).

taygahn [tAgan] v., love.

taykheboorkh [tAkebUrk] v., seek. Taykheboorkhtahn Tsahvahn, "Eternal Seeker".

taynee [tAnE] v., welcome.

tayr [tAr] v., help.

tayroo [tArU] adj., apparent(?), thorough(?).

tayroosh [tArUS] adv., apparently(?) thoroughly(?).

te [te] prep., by, with, in; of, among (cf. t', terth-).

-tee [-tE] suff., plural ("-s").

-tee [-tE] suff., 2nd pers. plur. actor ("you").

tee'ahnah [tE'ana] n., story-teller. Ti'ana, D'ni name of Anna.

teeg [tEg] v., work.

teegahl [tEgal] adj., working.

teeget [tEget] adj., working.

teegtahg [tEgtag] n., study. Also used as a suffix ("-ology").

teegtahn [tEgtan] n., worker.

teegtahv [tEgtav] n., work.

teejuh [tEju] n., [squad].

teemah [tEma] n., south. Kotsah Teemah, "South Gate".

tefoonet [tefUnet] n., memorial (cf. rifoon).

tel [tel] n., Guild.

telbahtsen [telbaxen] n., Guild of Cartographers (telokh bahtsentahntee).

telbeeree [telbErE] n., Guild of Maintainers (telokh beereetahntee).

telbetsiv [telbexiv] n., Guild of Engineers.

teldhoo'shol [telDU'Sol] n., Guild of Caterers (telokh doo'sholtahntee).

Teledahn [teleDan], lit. "Place of Mushroomy Spores" (to-elemartee-nadahnets).

telensho [telenSo] n., Guild of Tour Guides (telokh lenshotahntee).

telkailo [telKIlo] n., Guild of Healers.

telnahvah [telnava] n., Guild Master.

telook [telUK] n., Guild of Surveyors.

telookahm [telUKam] n., Surveyor.

telooknahvah [telUKnava] n., Surveyors Guild Master.

telrov [telrov] n., guildsman.

telshee [telSE] n., Guild of Messengers (telokh sheetemsootahntee).

tem [tem] n., ordinary ink (cf. lem "ink for Linking Books").

temah [tema] v., hear(?), heed(?).

temo [temo] prep. after(?), since(?) (cf. te "by", mo "that").

ten [ten] adj., simple.

Te'Negamiris [te'negamiris?] n., the great burial Age.

tenesh [teneS] adv., simply.

ter [ter] n., tree. Terahnee "New Tree".
Terokh Jeruth "Tree of Possibility".
Garternay "Root of the Great Tree".

terelin [terelin] n., contact.

terth [terT] prep., in a, of a, as a (cf. t', ehrth-).

tes [tes] n., group.

tetemo [tetemo] prep., onwards(?), afterwards(?) (cf. te, temo).

Tetsonot [texonot], lit. "in (the) abyss".

-th [-T] suff., adjective to noun ("-ty", "_ one") (cf. -eth).

thirk [TirK] v., save, keep.

thoe [Toe, ToE] adv., how?. Possibly an alternate spelling of dho.

Ti'ahnah [tE'ana] n., story-teller; Ti'ana (D'ni name of Anna).

tik [tiK] v., deny, refuse.

tikolee [tiKolE] n., [sorrow].

tikoleet [tiKolEt] adj., sorry.

tildah [tilDa] v., suffocate.

timel [timel] n., gallery.
Timelokh Kaydish "Kadish Gallery".

tishmah [tiSma] n., friend.

tiwah [tiwa] n., shaft.

to [to] n., place. Often used as prefix meaning "place of" (cf. following entries).

todelmer [toDelmer] n., planetarium
(to "place" + delahn "sky" + mer "to watch").

togitsah [togixa] n., haven
(to "place" + gitsah "safe").

togo [togo] n., floor.
Retogo kenen ahnoets "the floor is wet".

tokituh [toKitu] v., determine, be determined.

Tokotah [toKota], lit. "place of the locked door".

tolesah [tolesa] n., sealed place, vault.

tomahgilo [tomagilo] n., garden (cf. tomahn, gilo "plant").

tomahn [toman] n., house.

tomahnah [tomana] n., home.

tomahrah [tomara] n., concert hall (cf. mahrah).

tome [tome] adj., homesick (lit. "out of place").

tomet [tomet] adv., here (lit. "this place").

tomot [tomot] adv., there (lit. "that place").

tonah [tona] adj., long.

toogo [tUgo] n., foot.

tool [tUl] v., grow.

toomin [tUmin] adj., touched(?), handled(?), pressed(?).

toporpah [toporpa] n., palace.

tor [tor] num., 4, four.

toran [torån] n., unit of angular elevation, equal to 0.00576°; a right angle is 15,625 (25^3) torantee.

torekor [toreKor] n., library (lit. "place of the book").

torets [torex] num., fourth.

torinai [torinI] adj., cold.

torn [torn] v., spit.

totel [totel] n., Guild House.

tre- [tre-] prep., at the, in the, near the, with the, of the (cf. t', re-).

Tre'bivdil [tre'bivDil] n., lit. "in the everything".

trel [trel] adj., blue.

tren [tren] determ., a few, some.

trom [trom] n., wing.

tromets [tromex] adj., winged.

trov [trov] v., spin.

tsahn [xan] adv., always, forever.

tsahnlee [xanlE] n., mountain.

tsahnlee yahm [xanlE yam] n., iceberg (cf. yahm).

tsahno [xano] adj., everlasting, permanent, eternal (nonliving).

tsahnosh [xanoS] adv., permanently.

tsahnril [xanril] adv., never (lit. "always not").

tsahr [xar] v., go.

tsahroo [xarU] n./adj., eye(?), full(?).

tsahv [xav] v., live.

tsahvahn [xavan] adj., immortal, eternal (living).

tsahvteegtahg [xavtEgtag] n., biology.

tsaydor [xADor] v., [burrow].

tsaydortahn [xADortan] n., burrower, burrowing animal.

tseemah [xEma] v., need.

tseemahahl [xEmaal] adj., needed, necessary.

tso [xo] prep., of, about. Used to express non-personal relation.

tsofah [xofa] n., horn (of an animal).

tsogahl [xogal] adj., sunny, bright. Eder Tsogal, a Garden Age.

tsoid [xoiD] v., glow.

tsoidahl [xoiDal] adj., glowing.

tson [xon] n., [foundation].

tsonot [xonot] n., abyss (cf. Mayan tz'onot). Tetsonot, lit. "in the abyss".

tsoonoo [xUnU] v., greet.

tsootay [xUtA] v., dedicate(?), owe(?).

tsosahtahv [xosatav] n., possession.

tsotoy [xotO] n., child.

tuliema [tuliema] n., a plant native to Serenol, with three leaves that thrust through the earth into the air and turn a bright yellow hue at dawn.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>U

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>uhgraht [ugrat] n., pillars in the Riven wahrk lake, used to hung villagers to be fed to the wahrk as a form of punishment.

uru [UrU] n., large gathering; great community.

urwin [urwin?] n., a large animal native to Negilahn. Its primary food source is the kiri. The Payiferen 'sandscrit' is generally believed to be related to the urwin.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>V

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>vah- [va-] num., 5, five, combining form.

vahgahbree [vagabrE] num., 7, seven.

vahgahfah [vagafa] num., 6, six.

vahgahsen [vagasen] num., 8, eight.

vahgahtor [vagator] num., 9, nine.

vahkh [vak] adj., linking (cf. korvahkh "Linking Book").

vahmo [vamo] n., east.

vahmo [vamo] adj. calm.

vahmot [vamot] adj., eastern; pacific.

vaht [vat] num., 5, five.

vailee [vIlE] n., D'ni month, slightly longer than a Surface month. Divided into 29 yahrtee.

vaiuh [vIu] n., event(?), term(?).

vaynuh [vAnu] v., ask(?), explore(?).

vaytsoo [vAxU] n., presence.

veech [vEc] v., [scream].

veechtahv [vEctav] n., scream.

veelay [vElA] n., soul.

veewuh [vEwu] v., to deserve.

Venalem [venalem] n., ink-harvesting Age (cf. lem "ink").

veren [veren] v., mollify, pacify.

viduh [viDu] n., atmosphere.

vilekh [vilek] n., misery.

v'jah [v'ja] n., celebration (cf. Korfah V'ja "First Book Celebration").

vog [vog] n., nature.

vogets [vogex] adj., natural.

vokan [voKån] n., birth.

volah [vola] interj., yes.

voohee [vUhE] aux. v., can, could. Usually following the main verb: kenen voohee shuhteejoo "it could be rocksalt".

vor [vor] n., page (ordinary paper) (cf. bor "Linking Book page").

votahnah [votana] n., truth.

votahr [votar] v., praise.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>W

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>winis [winis] adv., together.

wish [wiS] v., lift, raise.

wotsah [woxa] adj., harsh.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>Y

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>yahm [yam] n., [ice] (cf. tsahnlee yahm "iceberg").

yahr [yar] n., D'ni day, equal to ~30 hr 14 min (1.26 Surface days). Divided into 5 gahrtahvotee.

Yahvo [yavo] n., Maker, God.

yayshah [yASa] n., joy.

yeepay [yEpA] n., eyeglasses, [goggles].

yeeshah [yESa] n., laughter.

yeret [yeret] aux. v., may. Usually following the main verb: Yahvo pilelen yeret veelayon "may Yahvo receive her soul".

yertis [yertis] n., a small plant native to Riven. Its yellow berries contain a neurotoxin used for hunting food.

yim [yim] v., see.

yimah [yima] adj., seen.

yishah [yiSa] n., [planet].

yoorach [yUråc] v., breathe.

yootay [yUtA] n., guinea pig.

yootay [yUtA] v., owe.


<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>Z

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>zahfay [zafA] n., fate.

zahg [zag] v., [prolong].

zahgah [zaga] adj., prolonged.

zander [zånDer] n., gravity.

zandni [zånDnE] n., Call to D'ni (zander + D'nee).

ze [ze] pron., her, him.

zeeglah [zEgla] adj., mad; insane, twisted, warped.

zeero [zEro] n., center(?), point of origin(?). Regahro Zeero "the Great Zero".

zeeway [zEwA] n., weather.

zik [ziK] n., [pod].

zintsahr [zinxar] v., escape(?), leave(?); deserve(?) (perhaps from tsahr "go").

zith [ziT] adj., low.

zithah [ziTa] adj., lowest(?), less than(?).

zithahth [ziTaT] n., [low(est) one, Least].

zithon [ziTon] v., [lower].

zo'e [zo'e] n., loss.

zoo [zU] pron., me.

zoodoo [zUDU] v., regret.

zuh [zu] n., end.

zuhnuh [zunu] n., ending.]]></translation>
            </element>
            <element name="DniDictED1">
                <translation language="English"><![CDATA[<cover src="DniDictED1.hsm"><font size=12 style=b face=courier color=000000><margin right=56 left=56 top=40 bottom=40><PB><p align=center>

