            <element name="DniDictRE">
                <translation language="English"><![CDATA[<cover src="DniDictRE.hsm"><font size=12 style=b face=courier color=000000><margin right=56 left=56 top=40 bottom=40><PB><p align=center>

Rivenese to English Dictionary<PB><PB>

<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>Abbreviations<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>

                   adj: adjective
                   adv: adverb
                   art: article
                   aux: auxiliary
                    cf: compare
                  conj: conjunction
                determ: determinative
                   fut: future
                     n: noun
                   num: number
                  perf: perfect
                  pers: person
                  plur: plural
                  pref: prefix
                  prep: preposition
                  pres: present
                  prog: progressive
                  pron: pronoun
               quantif: quantifier
                  sing: singular
                  suff: suffix
                     v: verb<PB><PB>

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>abi, v., love: abirakin "I love you".

aimo, n., woman.

ainela, n., flower; girl.

aki, adj., dangerous.

Allapo, n., water pool.

Allatwan, n., pool of stars (cf. latai "star").

anarapo, v., I praise: Gen anarapo "praise Gehn!" (lit. I praise Gehn).

atrapa, n., arm; branch (of a tree).


babi, v., cry, weep.

bela, n., [day] (cf. ohubela "celebration", vrebela "yesterday", yibela "afternoon").

buku, n., thing (generic).


cho, suff., whoa, hey. Verbal suffix indicates speaker is surprised by the action.

choli, n., sorrow, grief.


damai, v., laugh.

droi, v., carry.

duna, v., dig; paddle, row.


edre, adj., blue or green.

elari, adj., beautiful.


fari, adj., red.

fraita, adj., trapped; captured.


kelarapo, v., "I strike it".

kevisa, n., mill stone, quern.

kowa, adj., quiet, silent; a calm moment in the sea; a sunbreak.


latai, n., star; beloved.

lopa, v., shoot.

lopom, n., heart.


-me, suff., added to proverbial or gnomic statements ("everyone knows", "they say that").

mirimau, adj., joy, happiness.

miyu, n., story (usually spoken), an account of events.

mo, prep., one; with.


-n, suff., [you] (cf. abirakin "I love you", torilosan "they possibly discovered you").

navare, n., frame, edge of an opening.

nefatai, v., spark, ignite.

negen, v., pour (lit. "to cause [to] run").


ohubela, n., celebration (lit. "good-day").


palo, v., stand; to be in a temporary state of.

poloiya, v., escape.

puba, n., lip; edge; shore.

pumeko, n., whisper.


rahara, n., anger.

rauno, adj., strong in sensation (bright, loud, pungent, etc.); proud.

rekor, n., Linking book (cf. D'ni rekor "the book").


sadago, n., hide, leather, prepared skin of an animal.

safi, n., song.

ser, v., twist, coil.

serea, n., grain.

shicho, n., flying insect.

sraba, n., leaf; page.

srain, n., shadow.


take, v., take.

tapomo, n., window; eyepiece; doorway, opening; linking panel.

Tay, n., Age of the Moiety after escaping from Riven.

tewan, n., clear daytime sky.

tis, v., examine; read.

torilosan, v., "they possibly discovered you".

tuweda, n., memory.


ubin, n., knot; joint; place where paths meet.

usoi, n., bone.


vai, v., want, desire.

vrebela, n., yesterday.

vrirk, n., sliver, a small piece; a moment of time.

vuten, n., hide, skin (of an animal).


wahrk, n., large, tusked, carnivorous animal that prowls the oceans on Riven.

wan, n., sky(?); pool (?) (cf. tewan "clear daytime sky", wuwan "cloudy sky", Allatwan "pool of stars").

wipe, n., invader, interloper, unwanted guest.

wubo, n., cloud.

wusifa, n., prison; confinement.

wuwan, n., cloudy sky.


yibela, n., uncertain period of time, approximately the length of an afternoon.

ytram, n., froglike animal on Riven; Gehn captured the Ytrams and distilled them into a purified juice which he then smoked in his fire marble pipe.]]></translation>
            </element>
            <element name="DniDictER">
